Over an ensuing 14-season minor league odyssey, Cohen pitched at every minor league level between Class AAA and Class C.  High blood pressure relieved him from World War II military service. He also umpired for a season (1941) in the low-minor North Carolina State League. Thereafter, Syd posted double-digit win totals for the now Triple-A PCL Portland Beavers for four-consecutive seasons (1942-1945) and recorded his finest season (17-5, .773) for the El Paso Texans of the Arizona-Texas League in 1947. Before ending his playing career in at age 46 in 1952, Cohen also tried his hand at managing, guiding clubs in the Arizona-Texas League (1947, 1949-1950, 1952) and Southwest International League (1951), guiding the Ciudad Juarez (Mexico) Indios to the Arizona-Texas League crown in 1950.        
